+  // integers keep their type: ttnn's accumulation kernel takes max and min
+  // natively, and float32 cannot hold every int32. Like ttnn's elementwise
+  // max and min, it compares sign-magnitude bits: +NaN is the largest value
+  // and -NaN the smallest, so cummax propagates +NaN but cummin does not.
+  void replaceWithCumulativeReduction(
